        and focused. An industry is a group of firms producing products that are close
        substitutes for each other and serve the same customers. Thus, selecting the
        telecommunications industry may be too broad. The definition of the industry
        should be more focused, such as “the Internet service provider industry serv-
        ing homes and businesses in Ohio and Indiana.” If data are not available for the
        targeted area of the market, the closest proxy should be used. For example, if sta-
        tistics are not available for Ohio and Indiana, they may be available for the Mid-
        west or the United States. Then, define this market and describe the customer.
        The second step is to describe the regulatory and legal issues within the industry.
        Both national, as well as state and local regulations, should be considered. Also,
        changes in regulations can influence both industry-funding trends and particular
        types of companies within an industry [Sine et al., 2005].
